# apply-mode.conf — CV610 craft (.181). Install as
# /etc/waybeam-link/modes/apply-mode.conf alongside apply-mode.sh, which
# sources it. §15.5 forks the applier with execl() and no environment, so this
# file is the only place a craft can state how it differs.
#
# api, not init: S95waybeam's stop() ends in `$LOADER stop`, which unloads the
# ~25 open_* CV610 MPP modules. That takes the board off the network and needs
# a power cycle — so an init restart in flight is unrecoverable, where venc's
# own POST /api/v1/restart re-execs the daemon and leaves the loader alone.
VENC_RESTART=api
VENC_CTRL=127.0.0.1:80
